## 🔢 e. API Versioning Awareness

API versioning allows different versions of an API to exist when breaking changes are introduced.

For example:

```text
/api/v1/products/
/api/v2/products/
```

### Version 1

```text
GET /api/v1/products/
```

### Version 2

```text
GET /api/v2/products/
```

Different versions can support different response formats, fields, or behaviors.

### Why API Versioning Matters

API versioning helps:

- Maintain backward compatibility
- Introduce breaking changes safely
- Give clients time to migrate
- Support older applications
- Manage long-term API evolution

### Common Versioning Approaches

#### URL Versioning

```text
/api/v1/products/
/api/v2/products/
```

#### Query Parameter Versioning

```text
/api/products/?version=1
```

#### Header Versioning

```http
Accept: application/json; version=1
```

The exact versioning strategy depends on the API architecture and project requirements.

